# English identifiers, localized display

## Rule

**Everything that is not shown visually to the end user must be in English.**

Display-facing copy (labels, placeholders, button text, empty states, toast messages, `aria-label`) may use the product locale (Spanish in this app).

## Must be English

- Option / enum / preset `value` keys
- Variable, function, type, and file names
- Object keys and API/query param names in new code
- Route names, permission names, feature flags
- Test names and commit messages
- Comments and code documentation

## May be localized (display only)

- `label`, `text`, `placeholder`, `title`, `description`
- Visible button / menu / toast copy
- User-facing `aria-label` / `aria-labelledby` text

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ value English, label localized
{ value: "today", label: "Hoy" }
{ value: "week", label: "Esta Semana" }

// ❌ value in Spanish
{ value: "hoy", label: "Hoy" }
```

```ts
// ✅ non-visual keys in English
filters: { date: "today", date_range: ["2024-01-01", "2024-01-31"] }

// ❌ non-visual keys in Spanish
filters: { fecha: "hoy", rango_fecha: ["2024-01-01", "2024-01-31"] }
```

When touching legacy Spanish non-visual names (`fecha`, `rol`, DB columns, etc.), prefer migrating to English in the same change when practical; do not introduce new Spanish identifiers.
